## Goal
Fix DEV-48: links that apps wrap in redirects (Slack sign-in, Google `/url`, Outlook Safe Links, slack-redirect) were routed by the wrapper host, so e.g. a Jira link clicked in Slack fell into the default profile. Rules should match the real target.

## Problems
- The Slack Jira app hands macOS a `login_initiate_redirect` link whose real target sits inside a JWT claim, so a simple query parameter was not enough.
- Unwrapping parses untrusted input (base64, JSON), so it needs size limits, a depth limit and no panics.
- Several places call routing (URL handler, `open`, `rules match`, `/api/match`, Remember), and the log parser reads a fixed note column, so all had to learn the new note.
- Earlier tests and acceptance criteria never covered wrapped links.

## Decision
Added `internal/rules/unwrap.go`: no network, up to 3 nested levels, only http/https inner URLs with a host, the JWT signature unchecked and used only to pick a profile. Rules see the inner URL first; a rule on the wrapper host applies only when unwrapping fails. The browser still receives the original link so sign-in completes. Ask title and Remember key come from the inner URL. The decision log keeps the original URL in its URL column and appends `unwrapped <inner>` to the note. `rules match`, `--dry-run` and `/api/match` show the inner URL. The log tail and UI were updated, and `docs/rules.md` documents it. Any failure falls back to the old behaviour.

## Rejected
- Following redirects over the network: slow, leaks the click, unnecessary.
- Opening the inner URL directly: could break the Slack sign-in flow.
- Wrapper rule first: it would keep the bug.
- A new ADR: no existing ADR is affected.

## Touched
Slack, Google and Outlook Safe Links redirect formats; `docs/rules.md`; the decision log; the serve UI and API; Go standard library (`net/url`, `encoding/base64`, `encoding/json`).
